  "updatedAt": "2026-11-04T08:39:50.151526200Z",
  "notes": [
    "Host contention: two or more other agents ran PostgreSQL/SQL Server containers and builds on the same machine during every run; machine CPU averaged 88-100% (JVM view) during the E9 steady windows. All E6/E9 runs here finished BEFORE the shared heavy-build lock rule was announced (about 14:45 local), so they overlapped other lanes; 0 minutes were spent waiting for the lock.",
    "Test-harness workarounds (not adapter or engine changes): (1) product-api LeaseTable SQL rewritten by a JDBC proxy on Oracle (BIGINT -> NUMBER(19)) and SQL Server (IF NOT EXISTS, FOR UPDATE); without it neither adapter can be constructed on those DBs. (2) Flowable message correlation in E6 goes through RuntimeService because EngineAdapter.correlateMessage (Flowable) finds no execution for a catch event inside a parallel branch. (3) E9 starts Flowable's async executor and sets the history level on the built engine.",
    "Trial run with 4 concurrent fetchers (5 s warm-up, 15 s window, level full): Operaton adapter errors 17.4% of commands on R1 and 9.1% on R5 (duplicate key on spike_lease_pkey, StaleLeaseException, 'locked by worker-0', NotFoundException); 30 R1 and 28 R5 instances never ended. Flowable: 73/46 OLEs, all recovered by retry, 0 errors. The measured runs therefore use ONE fetcher feeding 4 completer threads on both engines.",
    "R5-lite throughput is bounded by the closed-loop driver (8 synthetic actors, 200 open instances; end-to-end ~16 s = Little's law 200/11.5 per s), not by either engine alone; compare command latencies, not instances/s, for R5.",
    "Runs: 13:56-14:10 local time."
  ]
